{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPxHrZ2sVmoLB9b6PvKm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've routed issue #321 with status **done**: next is `triage:engineer` and the worker is `engineer`. The issue adds an opt-in end-to-end test that runs the Kubernetes executor on a local kind cluster.\n\n**Why it isn't blocked:** the issue depends on #318, #319 and #320, and all three are now on main:\n- #318, the serve wiring, landed as part 7.\n- #319, the chart's jobs namespace and network policies, landed.\n- #320, the agent and pod images, landed.\n\n**Why only the engineer:** the only triage roles are lead and engineer, and the only worker is engineer. The only reviewer, eng-review, has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it reviews every pull request already and I didn't add it.\n\n**Open issues for a maintainer** (all in the file's comment body):\n- **Missing cluster script:** the issue expected #319 or a human PR to add a cluster-creation script under `deploy/`. #319 merged without one. `deploy/` is a protected path, so a PR that touches it needs human approval. The plan should either have the test create the cluster itself or wait for a human to add the script.\n- **CI workflow:** the workflow file goes under `.github/`, so a human has to add it.\n- **Design gap:** the done marker can be written by the agent, so one test case can't pass yet. The latest plan in the comments marks it pending, and a maintainer should confirm that's acceptable.\n- **Acceptance:** the worker's `make lint test` run only checks that the new test compiles. A human has to run `make kind-e2e`, which needs Docker, to accept the change.\n\nThe output is in `.ard/321/triage-lead.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":17690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_